<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barmakids</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Barmakid family, Barmakid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barmakids were a family of Iranian origin, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a>, who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a> and administrators to the early Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>. They held great influence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a>, patronising scholarship and organising government. In 803 Harun abruptly removed them from power, imprisoning and executing members of the family.</p></div>
